## Interface

One page, four panels, top to bottom. All interface text in English.

### Panel 1 — Journey summary (fixed, always visible)

Purpose statement and week counter.

Three figures, deliberately separate:

```
Curriculum    18 / 367 h     with progress bar
Projects            12 h     running total, no bar
Total               30 h     the motivation number
```

Curriculum has a finite target and gets a bar. Projects have no end state and
get a total. The combined figure belongs to neither and is the one worth
looking at daily.

Also: hours this week against the weekly target, current streak, and a link to
an external calendar.

### Panel 2 — Projects

One row per project: name, description, link, hours logged, log control.
A control to add a project.

Placed above the curriculum because it is the work being produced rather than
the material being consumed.

### Panel 3 — Curriculum

One collapsible block per module: name, month, and actual against planned hours
in the header.

Expanded, each resource row shows completion checkbox, name, link, description,
actual against planned hours, average usefulness rating, and a control to log a
session.

Resource completion is manual, never inferred from hours. Skipping a resource
on purpose is legitimate.

### Panel 4 — Weekly schedule

Reference only. Collapsed by default.

### Logging a session

Initiated from a resource row or a project row, never from a global form. The
target is therefore already known and never selected from a list.

Fields: date defaulting to today, minutes, rating where applicable, notes,
blocker.

